<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged by Tauri into the Info.plist of every macOS build, the DMG's and the
  Mac App Store's alike: a file named Info.plist next to tauri.conf.json is
  picked up without being named in any config.

  What Tauri writes itself and is therefore not here: CFBundleIdentifier, the
  versions, LSApplicationCategoryType (from bundle.category, Utility →
  public.app-category.utilities), NSHumanReadableCopyright,
  LSMinimumSystemVersion, NSHighResolutionCapable, and CFBundleURLTypes for
  uwurdp:// (from plugins.deep-link.desktop.schemes).

  - ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption true: UwURDP brings its own encryption, not
    only Apple's: TLS (rustls) and CredSSP/NTLM for RDP and the gateway,
    XChaCha20-Poly1305 with Argon2id for the vault, and end-to-end encrypted
    sync. All of it standard, published algorithms in open source code; the
    classification and what to answer in App Store Connect are in
    docs/app-store.md ("Export compliance").
  - NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription: macOS 15 asks before an app reaches the
    local network, which is where most RDP hosts are.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
  <true/>
  <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
  <string>UwURDP connects to the remote desktops and gateways you add, which are often on your local network.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
